<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Hosting Family for the Holidays? Rent Them a Car</h1>
<p>When visiting relatives have their own wheels, you skip the chauffeur runs and get more time at the table.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>One car, a full house, and five different schedules. If you're hosting relatives in Black River Falls for Thanksgiving or Christmas, someone always needs a ride: to see an old friend, to the store for the forgotten cranberries, to the deer stand at 5 AM. A rental car for your guests takes you out of the taxi business for the week.</p>
<h2>Why it works</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Everyone keeps their own schedule.</strong> Grandma's church service and your nephew's late night out no longer compete for one set of keys.</li>
<li><strong>Arrivals get easier.</strong> Relatives flying into La Crosse or Eau Claire still need a ride the last stretch. Pick them up once, and they handle the rest of the week themselves.</li>
<li><strong>Your own car stays home.</strong> No borrowed-car awkwardness about seat settings, gas, or who dinged the bumper.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What your guest needs to rent</h2>
<p>The renter needs to be <strong>21 or older</strong> (there's no young-driver fee), and needs three things: a valid U.S. driver's license, a credit or debit card (Visa, Mastercard, or Discover) linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance showing the policy number and expiration date. A security deposit, starting at $300, is held separately from the rental charges. We'll confirm the exact amount when you book. The <a href="/blog/what-you-need-to-rent-a-car-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">first-timer's guide</a> walks through it.</p>
<h2>Which rate applies</h2>
<p>Local renters get unlimited mileage on published local rates: $55/day or $330/week for an intermediate car, $65/day or $390/week for a full-size, and $80/day or $480/week for an SUV or the AWD Outback. Non-local rates are intermediate $75/day or $450/week, full-size $85/day or $510/week, and SUV/AWD $100/day or $600/week, plus a per-mile charge. Call 715-396-1466 for the per-mile rate. Local means residents of Black River Falls and Jackson County, WI. Not sure which applies to your guest? Call and we'll tell you before you book.</p>
<p>For a holiday visit, the weekly rate is usually the smart play. Wednesday to Wednesday costs less than paying day by day for five or six days. See <a href="/blog/weekly-car-rental-rates-when-7-days-beats-daily.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">when weekly beats daily</a>.</p>
<h2>Book early, and plan around holiday hours</h2>
<p>Thanksgiving week shares the calendar with the gun deer opener (Saturday, November 21), so SUVs and the AWD Outback go fast. <strong>We're closed Thanksgiving Day, Thursday, November 26,</strong> so plan pickups by Wednesday. Hours can also shift around Christmas Eve and New Year's Eve, so call to confirm pickup and return times for those weeks. Our regular hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> and we'll have your guests' car ready when they roll into town.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can my out-of-town relative rent a car from you?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, if they are 21 or older and bring a valid U.S. driver&#x27;s license, a Visa, Mastercard, or Discover credit or debit card linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance with the policy number and expiration date.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is there a young-driver fee?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>No. The minimum renter age is 21 and there is no under-25 fee.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do visiting relatives pay local or non-local rates?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Local rates apply to residents of Black River Falls and Jackson County, WI. Non-local rates are intermediate $75/day or $450/week, full-size $85/day or $510/week, and SUV/AWD $100/day or $600/week, plus a per-mile charge. Call 715-396-1466 for the per-mile rate. Call and we&#x27;ll confirm which rate applies before you book.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How far ahead should I book a car for holiday guests?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Two to three weeks ahead for Thanksgiving and Christmas. Thanksgiving week overlaps the gun deer opener, so SUVs and the AWD Outback book up first.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
